# capability_evolution.run_controlled_experiment() (2026-09-05) writes each
# isolated baseline/treatment fixture run under here -- ~67 untracked files
# per real experiment run, per the three-loop gap-close review's own
# measurement. Per-run scratch, never a deliverable.
.dv-harness/experiments/

# Local-only credential script for relay auto-reconnect (CLAUDE.md 2026-09-03
# amendment) -- must never be committed, this machine only.
replay.ps1

# Local DuckDB evidence store (evidence-db-wiring, 2026-09-03, default-ON --
# see dv_harness/config.py's evidence_db block and dv_harness/evidence_db.py).
# Generated locally by every reconciliation cycle; a multi-MB binary file
# with no place in version control.
.dv-harness/evidence/

# Per-run harness RUNTIME STATE under .dv-harness/ (2026-09-03). Everything
# below is rewritten continuously by a live session -- the LSF watcher's PID
# file and log (dv-harness lsf-watch-start), the blackboard's current-truth
# snapshots, the engine's own state/event journal -- so it churns on every
# run and belongs to the machine it was produced on, not to version control.
# Only .dv-harness/evidence/ was previously excluded, which left a careless
# `git add -A` free to sweep a stale watcher.pid (and a multi-MB watcher.log)
# into an unrelated commit.
#
# Two honest caveats, both verified against `git ls-files` on 2026-09-03
# rather than assumed:
#  1. .dv-harness/state.json, .dv-harness/events.jsonl, and several files
#     under .dv-harness/lsf/ and .dv-harness/blackboard/ are ALREADY TRACKED
#     from earlier commits. .gitignore does not apply to tracked files, so
#     their modifications still show in `git status` and can still be staged.
#     These lines stop NEW runtime files from being swept in; they are not a
#     substitute for never running `git add -A` / `git add .dv-harness`.
#     Untracking the already-tracked ones is a separate, deliberate decision
#     (`git rm --cached`) that has not been made here.
#  2. Real, intentionally-versioned content does live under these paths
#     (lsf/*_policy.json, lsf/job_state_schema.json, the blackboard's seed
#     *_state.json files). Add such a file explicitly with `git add -f` --
#     it will not be picked up automatically any more.
.dv-harness/lsf/
.dv-harness/blackboard/
.dv-harness/state.json
.dv-harness/events.jsonl

# Stage-boundary progress reports (2026-09-04,
# dv_harness/stage_progress_display.py -- save_stage_report()). Two markdown
# files are written per stage ATTEMPT, named by timestamp, so a single real
# workflow run over the 39-stage order leaves dozens of new files and a
# retried stage adds two more each time. Same reasoning as the runtime state
# above: a per-machine record of what this run displayed, not shared history.
# They are meant to be read where they were produced -- `dv-harness
# stage-report <stage>` re-renders the latest, `--list` shows them all.
.dv-harness/stage_reports/

# Harness self-test run records (2026-09-04, tools/testing/self_test.py
# --record; written by the pre-push hook's self-test gate and by CI). Same
# reasoning as the runtime state above: an append-only per-machine execution
# log, rewritten on every push, that answers "did an automated trigger
# actually run the self-test on THIS machine" -- which is a local question,
# not shared history. Read it with `cat .dv-harness/self_test/last_run.json`.
.dv-harness/self_test/

# USB_UVM_Handoff (2026-09-04) -- the canonical structural reference tree
# named in CLAUDE.md's "Architecture-conformance audit" section, consolidated
# into this repo at the user's request so an agent doesn't need to reach
# outside the project tree to check structural conformance / post-hoc
# fidelity. Read-only, reference-only per CLAUDE.md's "No Golden-Reference
# Content Mining" rule -- the real EVIDENCE_QUOTE_NOT_FOUND_IN_FILE gate
# (dv_harness/prompts.py) still fails any generation evidence quote whose
# path resolves under this directory, unchanged by this consolidation.
# Excluded from git because the tree itself contains real internal
# identifiers (service accounts, internal hostnames) from the original DE
# handoff -- the same class of data this repo's own history was cleaned of
# on 2026-09-04. Present on disk, never in version control.
reference/USB_UVM_Handoff/

# Throwaway scratch/probe trees under .work/ (2026-09-05) -- synthetic
# projects created by test/E2E-demo scripts this session
# (.work/e2e_usb3_lfps_demo.py and several ad-hoc CLI probes) to exercise a
# real code path against a disposable .dv-harness tree, never meant to be
# committed. A leading underscore is this project's own convention for such
# throwaway dirs (see .work/_p25_probe*, .work/_e2e_demo_usb3_lfps,
# .work/_review_amba_e2e, .work/audit_tmp_project, .work/rp_cli_check).
.work/_*/
.work/_*
.work/audit_tmp_project/
.work/rp_cli_check/

# Raw scratch dumps this session -- journal-style intermediate logs kept
# only to unblock a specific in-progress audit/gap-close step, never a
# deliverable in their own right (the actual finding lands in a real
# gap-close-*.md report instead). Underscore-prefixed ones are already
# covered by `.work/_*` above.
.work/*_journal_*.txt

# More per-machine runtime state (2026-09-05), same reasoning as the
# .dv-harness/lsf|blackboard|state.json|events.jsonl block above: rewritten
# continuously, a record of THIS machine's run, not shared history.
# - .dv-harness/react/: Working Memory reasoning-step records -- per
#   CLAUDE.md's own Engineering Memory Policy, Working Memory is short-term
#   reasoning context, "預設不永久保存" (not permanently stored by default).
# - .dv-harness/self_tuning/: the autonomous gate self-tuning gate_history.jsonl.
# - .dv-harness/telemetry/: per-run workflow/stage timing profile.
# - .dv-harness/sessions/_pre_restore_*/: timestamped pre-restore session
#   backup snapshots.
.dv-harness/react/
.dv-harness/self_tuning/
.dv-harness/telemetry/
.dv-harness/sessions/_pre_restore_*/

# Full extracted text of official third-party protocol specifications
# (2026-09-05: USB 2.0/3.2, UTMI, xHCI -- .work/pdftxt/, produced by a PDF
# text-extraction pass this session). A copyright concern distinct from the
# internal-identifier class of data this repo's history was cleaned of:
# redistributing full official spec text is not this project's call to make.
# Present on disk for local reference, never in version control.
.work/pdftxt/

# The DV-Knowledge Vault (dv_harness/memory_vault.py) is its OWN git
# repository as of 2026-09-04, when this project turned on
# `memory.git_enabled` in .dv-harness/config.json -- that is the entire
# point of the "Markdown + Git" design: every real memory promotion commits
# its own note with a `memory(<protocol>): ...` message, inside the vault.
# It was already untracked-but-not-ignored here (confirmed via `git
# check-ignore` before this line was added, so nothing is being untracked by
# it). Now that a real .git tree lives inside it, leaving it merely
# untracked would let a `git add -A` embed it in THIS repo as a bare gitlink
# -- a commit pointing at a SHA no clone can resolve. Browse its history
# with `git -C .dv-harness/vault log --oneline`.
.dv-harness/vault/

# GUI-19 (2026-09-05): dashboard_session.json carries a live, per-session
# auth token minted by dashboard_auth.issue_session_token() -- the same
# class of secret the Engineering Memory Policy above forbids persisting
# into any tracked artifact. Every sibling runtime-state file (state.json,
# events.jsonl, blackboard/, lsf/) is already ignored; this one was missed,
# and this session's own gap-close pass showed loose untracked files get
# swept into unrelated commits (e0a3002) -- exactly the failure mode this
# line prevents.
.dv-harness/dashboard_session.json

# NTFS alternate-data-stream artifacts from Windows-illegal `:` filenames
# an agent attempted this session (gap-close-gui-gui-09:-report.md etc.) --
# the colon was stripped for the real report, but a stray zero-byte file
# using the original name remains on disk and is not covered by the
# .work/_* scratch rule above.
.work/gap-close-gui-gui-09
.work/gap-close-gui-gui-19

